From 7460275581613eb2ed48f3832af9dbd8f8259fe4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam Day <me@samcday.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 20:41:44 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] policy: refuse host_mode while a preserved foreign
 gadget is bound

foreign_gadgets = "preserve" promises that usb-signaller never touches a
gadget it did not create, but check_host_mode let host_mode through for
such a gadget. Host role removes the UDC and so unbinds every gadget on
it: a preserved gadget that serves the root filesystem, but is not
declared, took the root filesystem with it.

check_host_mode now refuses host_mode while a foreign gadget is bound
under "preserve", before any role is written. get_modes reuses the check
and no longer offers host_mode in that state. A broken configuration
keeps its own, more specific, message.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
